IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cp5-months`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division F (Reconsiderations and Appeals): sections 81 to 86.1.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- A person who is dissatisfied with a decision about their benefit may ask the Minister to reconsider it (section 81), appeal
-- the Minister's decision to the Social Security Tribunal (section 82), and may have a benefit stayed while a Tribunal
-- decision is contested (section 83). Sections 84 to 86.1 are repealed.
-- The Regulations (piece cr2) fix the form of the request (regulation 74.1(1)), how the person must be notified
-- (regulation 74.2) and when the Minister may allow a longer period (regulation 74.1(3) and (4)). They are read here so that
-- "am I in time?" has an answer, and cr2 encodes the regulations themselves.
-- The time for an appeal under section 82 and for leave to appeal is set by the Department of Employment and Social
-- Development Act, which is not among the texts this encoding reads.

-- out of range: sections 55, 55.1 and 55.2 (piece cp3) and 55.3, 60 and 65.1 (piece cp4): the decisions that subsection 81(1) names, carried as a choice from a list
-- out of range: regulations 74, 74.1 and 74.2 (piece cr2): read in s 81(1)
-- out of range: section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act and the Federal Courts Act (not among the texts read): the Social Security Tribunal and the periods for leave and for judicial review in s 82 and s 83, plain inputs

§ `Part II, Division F -- Reconsiderations and appeals (sections 81 to 86.1)`

§§ `Subsection 81(1) -- who may ask the Minister to reconsider, and about what`

-- src:2484 | Appeal to Minister
-- src:2485 | 81 (1) Where
-- src:2486 | (a) a spouse, former spouse, common-law partner, former common-law partner or estate is dissatisfied with any decision made under section 55, 55.1, 55.2 or 55.3,
-- src:2487 | (b) an applicant is dissatisfied with any decision made under section 60,
-- src:2488 | (c) a beneficiary is dissatisfied with any determination as to the amount of a benefit payable to the beneficiary or as to the beneficiary’s eligibility to receive a benefit,
-- src:2489 | (d) a beneficiary or the beneficiary’s spouse or common-law partner is dissatisfied with any decision made under section 65.1, or
-- src:2490 | (e) a person who made a request under section 70.1, a child of that person or, in relation to that child, a person or agency referred to in section 75 is dissatisfied with any decision made under section 70.1,
-- src:2491 | the dissatisfied party or, subject to the regulations, any person on behalf thereof may, within ninety days after the day on which the dissatisfied party was notified in the prescribed manner of the decision or determination, or within such longer period as the Minister may either before or after the expiration of those ninety days allow, make a request to the Minister in the prescribed form and manner for a reconsideration of that decision or determination.
@ref Act s 81(1)(a) to (e) (src:2486-2490)
DECLARE `cp5 Person dissatisfied under subsection 81(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a spouse, former spouse, common-law partner, former common-law partner or estate dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(a)`
    `an applicant dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(b)`
    `a beneficiary dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(c) or (d)`
    `a beneficiary's spouse or common-law partner dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(d)`
    `a person who made a request under section 70.1, a child of that person or, in relation to that child, a person or agency referred to in section 75, dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(e)`
    `a person to whom none of paragraphs 81(1)(a) to (e) refers`

@ref Act s 81(1)(a) to (e) (src:2486-2490)
DECLARE `cp5 Decision or determination of subsection 81(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a decision made under section 55, 55.1, 55.2 or 55.3 that subsection 81(1) names`
    `a decision made under section 60 that subsection 81(1) names`
    `a determination as to the amount of a benefit payable to the beneficiary or as to the beneficiary's eligibility to receive a benefit that subsection 81(1) names`
    `a decision made under section 65.1 that subsection 81(1) names`
    `a decision made under section 70.1 that subsection 81(1) names`
    `a decision that subsection 81(1) does not name`

@ref Act s 81(1) (src:2485-2491)
GIVEN person IS A `cp5 Person dissatisfied under subsection 81(1)`
      decision IS A `cp5 Decision or determination of subsection 81(1)`
      `the person is dissatisfied with the decision or determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) — the person is a dissatisfied party who may ask the Minister to reconsider the decision or determination` person decision `the person is dissatisfied with the decision or determination` MEANS
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision or determination`
    AND (CONSIDER person
         -- (a) a spouse, former spouse, common-law partner, former common-law partner or estate dissatisfied with a decision made under section 55, 55.1, 55.2 or 55.3
         WHEN `a spouse, former spouse, common-law partner, former common-law partner or estate dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(a)` THEN decision EQUALS `a decision made under section 55, 55.1, 55.2 or 55.3 that subsection 81(1) names`
         -- (b) an applicant dissatisfied with a decision made under section 60
         WHEN `an applicant dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(b)` THEN decision EQUALS `a decision made under section 60 that subsection 81(1) names`
         -- (c) a beneficiary dissatisfied with a determination of the amount of a benefit or of eligibility
         WHEN `a beneficiary dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(c) or (d)` THEN
             (decision EQUALS `a determination as to the amount of a benefit payable to the beneficiary or as to the beneficiary's eligibility to receive a benefit that subsection 81(1) names`)
             -- (d) a beneficiary dissatisfied with a decision made under section 65.1
             OR (decision EQUALS `a decision made under section 65.1 that subsection 81(1) names`)
         -- (d) the beneficiary's spouse or common-law partner dissatisfied with a decision made under section 65.1
         WHEN `a beneficiary's spouse or common-law partner dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(d)` THEN decision EQUALS `a decision made under section 65.1 that subsection 81(1) names`
         -- (e) a person who made a request under section 70.1, a child of that person or a section 75 person or agency, dissatisfied with a decision made under section 70.1
         WHEN `a person who made a request under section 70.1, a child of that person or, in relation to that child, a person or agency referred to in section 75, dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(e)` THEN decision EQUALS `a decision made under section 70.1 that subsection 81(1) names`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- "or, subject to the regulations, any person on behalf thereof": the regulations (regulation 74, piece cr2) allow a person
-- authorized by or under a law, or considered qualified by the Minister, to act for a person who cannot manage their affairs.
@ref Act s 81(1) (src:2491)
GIVEN `the person is the dissatisfied party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations allow the person to make the request on behalf of the dissatisfied party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) — the person may make the request for the dissatisfied party` `the person is the dissatisfied party` `the regulations allow the person to make the request on behalf of the dissatisfied party` MEANS
    `the person is the dissatisfied party` OR `the regulations allow the person to make the request on behalf of the dissatisfied party`

§§ `Subsections 81(1) and (1.1) -- the time for the request`

-- Regulation 74.2: a notification referred to in subsection 81(1) or (1.1) must be in writing and sent by the Minister.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:738 | 74.2 A notification referred to in subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act must be in writing and sent by the Minister.
@ref Reg 74.2 (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:738)
GIVEN `the notice was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was sent by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) — the person was notified in the prescribed manner under regulation 74.2` `the notice was in writing` `the notice was sent by the Minister` MEANS
    `the notice was in writing` AND `the notice was sent by the Minister`

-- "within ninety days after the day on which the dissatisfied party was notified in the prescribed manner of the decision or
-- determination, or within such longer period as the Minister may either before or after the expiration of those ninety days allow".
-- Until the person has been notified in the prescribed manner the ninety days have not begun to run (NOTES.md, fork F15).
@ref Act s 81(1), s 81(1.1) (src:2491), (src:2493)
GIVEN `day notified in the prescribed manner` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 81(1) and (1.1) — the last day of the ninety days for the request` `day notified in the prescribed manner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `day notified in the prescribed manner`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST notified THEN JUST (`the date a time limit ends` notified (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90))

@ref Act s 81(1), s 81(1.1) (src:2491), (src:2493)
GIVEN `day notified in the prescribed manner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `last day of any longer period the Minister has allowed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `day the request is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) and (1.1) — the request for reconsideration is made in time` `day notified in the prescribed manner` `last day of any longer period the Minister has allowed` `day the request is made` MEANS
        (CONSIDER `s 81(1) and (1.1) — the last day of the ninety days for the request` `day notified in the prescribed manner`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST last THEN `day the request is made` AT MOST last)
     OR (CONSIDER `last day of any longer period the Minister has allowed`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST longer THEN `day the request is made` AT MOST longer)

-- Regulation 74.1(3) and (4): when the Minister may allow a longer period.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:731 | (3) For the purposes of subsections 81(1) and (1.1) of the Act and subject to subsection (4), the Minister may allow a longer period to make a request for reconsideration of a decision or determination if the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period and the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:732 | (4) The Minister must also be satisfied that the request for reconsideration has a reasonable chance of success, and that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period to make the request, if the request for reconsideration
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:733 | (a) is made after the 365-day period after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination;
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:734 | (b) is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit; or
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:735 | (c) is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3) of the Act.
@ref Reg 74.1(3), (4) (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:731-735)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made after the 365-day period after the day the person was notified in writing of the decision or determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the request has a reasonable chance of success` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) — the Minister may allow a longer period to make the request, under regulation 74.1(3) and (4)` `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period` `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration` `the request is made after the 365-day period after the day the person was notified in writing of the decision or determination` `the request is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit` `the request is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3)` `the Minister is satisfied that the request has a reasonable chance of success` `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period`
    AND `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration`
    -- (4): in the three cases it names, the Minister must also be satisfied of a reasonable chance of success and of no prejudice
    AND (   (NOT (   `the request is made after the 365-day period after the day the person was notified in writing of the decision or determination`
                  OR `the request is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit`
                  OR `the request is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3)`))
         OR (    `the Minister is satisfied that the request has a reasonable chance of success`
             AND `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period`))

-- Regulation 74.1(1): the request is made in writing to the Minister and sets out the contributor's name, address and Social Insurance
-- Number; the requester's name, address and relationship if not the contributor; and the grounds and the facts they rest on.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:726 | 74.1 (1) A request for a reconsideration under subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act shall be made in writing to the Minister and shall set out
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:727 | (a) the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor;
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:728 | (b) if the person making the request for the reconsideration is not the contributor, that person’s name and address and their relationship to the contributor; and
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:729 | (c) the grounds for the request for the reconsideration and a statement of the facts that form the basis of that request.
@ref Reg 74.1(1) (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:726-729)
GIVEN `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the request is the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out the name and address of the person making it and their relationship to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets out the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts that form its basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) — the request is made in the prescribed form and manner of regulation 74.1(1)` `the request is made in writing to the Minister` `the request sets out the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor` `the person making the request is the contributor` `the request sets out the name and address of the person making it and their relationship to the contributor` `the request sets out the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts that form its basis` MEANS
        `the request is made in writing to the Minister`
    AND `the request sets out the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor`
    AND (`the person making the request is the contributor` OR `the request sets out the name and address of the person making it and their relationship to the contributor`)
    AND `the request sets out the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts that form its basis`

§§ `Subsection 81(1.1) -- a penalty assessed under section 90.1`

-- src:2492 | Reconsideration where penalty assessed
-- src:2493 | (1.1) A person to whom a penalty has been assessed under section 90.1 or, subject to the regulations, any person on their behalf, who is dissatisfied with the decision to impose a penalty or with the amount of the penalty may, within 90 days after the day on which the person is notified in the prescribed manner of the decision or determination, or within any longer period that the Minister may, either before or after the expiration of those 90 days, allow, request, in the prescribed form and manner, that the Minister reconsider that decision or determination.
@ref Act s 81(1.1) (src:2493)
GIVEN `a penalty has been assessed on the person under section 90.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is dissatisfied with the decision to impose the penalty or with the amount of the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(1.1) — the person may ask the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or its amount` `a penalty has been assessed on the person under section 90.1` `the person is dissatisfied with the decision to impose the penalty or with the amount of the penalty` MEANS
    `a penalty has been assessed on the person under section 90.1` AND `the person is dissatisfied with the decision to impose the penalty or with the amount of the penalty`

§§ `Subsections 81(2) and (3) -- what the Minister does`

-- src:2494 | Reconsideration by Minister and decision
-- src:2495 | (2) The Minister shall reconsider without delay any decision or determination referred to in subsection (1) or (1.1) and may confirm or vary it, and may approve payment of a benefit, determine the amount of a benefit or determine that no benefit is payable, and shall notify in writing the party who made the request under subsection (1) or (1.1) of the Minister’s decision and of the reasons for it.
@ref Act s 81(2) (src:2495)
GIVEN `a request has been made under subsection (1) or (1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(2) — the Minister must reconsider the decision or determination without delay and notify the requester in writing of the decision and of the reasons for it` `a request has been made under subsection (1) or (1.1)` MEANS
    `a request has been made under subsection (1) or (1.1)`

-- src:2496 | Rescission or amendment of decision
-- src:2497 | (3) The Minister may, on new facts, rescind or amend a decision made by him or her under this Act.
@ref Act s 81(3) (src:2497)
GIVEN `there are new facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81(3) — the Minister may rescind or amend the decision` `there are new facts` MEANS
    `there are new facts`

§§ `Section 82 -- appeal to the Social Security Tribunal`

-- src:2498 | Appeal to Social Security Tribunal
-- src:2499 | 82 A party who is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 81, including a decision in relation to further time to make a request, or, subject to the regulations, any person on their behalf, may appeal the decision to the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref Act s 82 (src:2499)
GIVEN `the party is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 81` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 82 — the party may appeal the decision of the Minister to the Social Security Tribunal` `the party is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 81` MEANS
    `the party is dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 81`

§§ `Section 83 -- stay of benefits pending judicial review`

-- src:2500 | Stay of benefits pending judicial review
-- src:2501 | 83 If a decision is made by the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in respect of a benefit, the Minister may stay payment of the benefit until the latest of
-- src:2502 | (a) the expiry of the period allowed for making an application for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division of that Tribunal,
-- src:2503 | (b) the expiry of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision, and
-- src:2504 | (c) if Her Majesty has made an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision, the month in which all proceedings in relation to the judicial review have been completed.
@ref Act s 83 (src:2501-2504)
GIVEN `the Social Security Tribunal has made a decision in respect of the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `last day of the period allowed for making an application for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division` IS A DATE
      `last day of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month in which all proceedings in relation to a judicial review applied for by Her Majesty have been completed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 83 — the last day to which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` `the Social Security Tribunal has made a decision in respect of the benefit` `last day of the period allowed for making an application for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division` `last day of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision` `a day in the month in which all proceedings in relation to a judicial review applied for by Her Majesty have been completed` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Social Security Tribunal has made a decision in respect of the benefit`
    THEN NOTHING
    -- the latest of (a), (b) and (c); (c) is a month, taken as ending on the last day of that month (NOTES.md, fork F14)
    ELSE JUST (`cp5 helper -- the later of two days` (`cp5 helper -- the later of two days` `last day of the period allowed for making an application for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division` `last day of the period allowed for making an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision`) lastDayOfProceedings)
    WHERE
        lastDayOfProceedings MEANS CONSIDER `a day in the month in which all proceedings in relation to a judicial review applied for by Her Majesty have been completed`
                                   WHEN NOTHING THEN `last day of the period allowed for making an application for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division`
                                   WHEN JUST d THEN (`the month following the month of a date` d) PLUS (0 MINUS 1)
